  "metadata": {
    "title": "Precision Beef - Animal Behaviour Classification",
    "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.4064802",
    "publication_date": "2021-06-09",
    "description": "<p>The data set contains sensor data for three cattle behaviours, (<code>Eating</code>, <code>Rumination</code> and <code>Other</code>). In particular, it contains 18 animals over three farm trials in the Easter Howgate Farm, Edinburgh, UK.</p>\n\n<p>Each animal is assigned a unique identifier <code>XX</code> in the range <code>01</code>-<code>18</code> and is equipped with 2 devices:</p>\n\n<ol>\n\t<li>Afimilk Silent Herdsman Collar that provides the raw acceleration traces from a 3-axis MEMs accelerometer at frequency of 10 Hz.</li>\n\t<li>Rumiwatch Halter device that measures the pressure created by the jaw movements and provides classifications at frequency of 10 Hz.</li>\n</ol>\n\n<p>A detailed description of the data is provided in the <code>Readme.md</code>.</p>",
